## Architecture

### Keep OneShot structure or adopt Strands structure?

**Keep OneShot's structure. Use Strands as an adapter at the single model boundary.** Here is the decisive architectural fact that governs everything below:

> **OneShot is NOT an agent-loop system. It is a deterministic pipeline with exactly ONE LLM call.** I verified this directly:
> - `generateText` (the only model call) appears in **exactly one file**: `backend/agents/researcher/workflow.ts:3,144`.
> - Planner (`planner/workflow.ts`), Refactor, Evaluation, GapAnalysis are **deterministic** (coverage analysis, audit application, plan evaluation — no model).
> - TripleValidation runs **deterministic Python validation** (`triple-validation.ts`).
> - Confirmation/Hash are **deterministic** (assembly + SHA-256).
> - Builder runs a **hardened sandbox** (`BuilderWorkflow` → `SandboxService`), not a model.
>
> Strands is an **agent loop** (model → tool → context → repeat) plus multi-agent orchestration. So a 1:1 mapping is wrong: only the Researcher maps to a Strands `Agent`; the other 9 stages are deterministic processors that must NOT become agents (doing so would inject nondeterminism where AGENTS.md mandates deterministic validation — a hard invariant).

### Minimum changes to be Strands-compatible?

The linchpin is Strands' **`VercelModel` adapter** (`@strands-agents/sdk/models/vercel`), verified from the installed package's type defs:

```ts
// node_modules/@strands-agents/sdk/dist/src/models/vercel.d.ts (verbatim doc example)
import { VercelModel } from '@strands-agents/sdk/models/vercel'
const agent = new Agent({ model: new VercelModel({ provider: bedrock('...') }) })
for await (const event of agent.stream('Hello!')) { ... }
```

`VercelModel` wraps **any** `@ai-sdk/provider` `LanguageModelV3`. OneShot's `resolveActiveIntegrationModel()` (`backend/integration/runtime.ts:139`) **already returns** a `LanguageModelV3` (the output of `@ai-sdk/google|openai|anthropic`'s `factory(opts)(model)`). So the bridge is:

```ts
new VercelModel({ provider: active.model })   // active.model is already a LanguageModelV3
```

**Zero provider reimplementation.** The minimum change is: in the Researcher, optionally wrap the existing resolved model in `VercelModel` and call it via a Strands `Agent` instead of `generateText`. Everything else stays.

