## Stage 1: Single-Agent vs Multi-Agent

The prompt offers Option A (one Agent, 8 tools) and Option B (8 chained Agents). **Both are wrong for OneShot**, for the same root reason: 7 of 8 stages are deterministic and must not gain an LLM call.

| Option | What it implies | Verdict for OneShot |
|---|---|---|
| A — One Agent with 8 tools (INTENT/GENERATOR/etc. as tools) | An LLM agent *decides* which stage-tool to call next. | ❌ **Breaks determinism.** OneShot's stage order is fixed (`canonical-transition.ts`), with two human gates and a SHA-256 hash proof. Letting a model choose the next "stage tool" would make the workflow nondeterministic and destroy the hash-equality guarantee (`hash.ts`). The "8 stages" are also wrong (real workflow has ~10 stages, no GENERATOR). |
| B — 8 Agents chained (each stage an Agent) | Each stage = an LLM agent. | ❌ **Adds 7 spurious LLM calls.** Planner/Refactor/Evaluation/GapAnalysis/TripleValidation/Confirmation/Hash are deterministic by design. Wrapping them in Strands `Agent`s would call a model where none should exist, violating "deterministic validation" and "do not fabricate progress" invariants. Also, Strands `Graph` nodes are agents — but OneShot's deterministic nodes aren't agents. |
| **C (correct, not listed)** — **One Strands `Agent` for the ONE model-driven stage (Researcher); deterministic pipeline unchanged.** | Strands adapts the model boundary only. | ✅ **Matches the approved plan** ("Strands as adapter, not replacement"). Reuses `resolveActiveIntegrationModel()` via `VercelModel`. Keeps `backend/pipeline/` + `backend/workflow/` as the orchestrator. |

**Recommendation: Option C.** Use Strands `Agent` *only* for the Researcher's draft generation. The canonical transition table (`canonical-transition.ts`) remains the single source of truth for stage movement; Strands is never the orchestrator.

If a *future* requirement adds more LLM stages, each would become its own Strands `Agent` (still not tools, still not a Graph — because the deterministic gating/hash logic must stay in OneShot's pipeline).

