## Stage 5: Streaming

**Current mechanism**: SSE (`GET /api/runs/:id/events`, `http-server.ts:1258-1305`), payload = `ProcessingEvent` (workflow stage events, **not** model tokens). The model call itself is non-streaming (`generateText`, `workflow.ts:144`). Strands TS streaming is **`agent.stream()`** (an `AsyncGenerator<AgentStreamEvent, AgentResult>`), **not** `stream_async` (that's the Python SDK).

Adapter that pipes Strands stream → OneShot's existing SSE channel (provider-agnostic by construction — `VercelModel` normalizes all providers):

```ts
// NEW FILE (optional UX enhancement): backend/agents/researcher/strands-streaming.ts
import { Agent } from "@strands-agents/sdk";
import type { ProcessingEventBus } from "../../runtime/event-bus.js";

export async function streamResearcherDraft(
  agent: Agent,
  promptText: string,
  runId: string,
  events: ProcessingEventBus,
): Promise<string> {
  let text = "";
  // agent.stream() yields AgentStreamEvent; the generator's return value is the AgentResult
  const gen = agent.stream(promptText);
  while (true) {
    const { value, done } = await gen.next();
    if (done) {
      // gen return value is AgentResult; use its text/structuredOutput
      const result = value as any;
      return text || result?.toString?.() || "";
    }
    const event = value as any;
    // Forward text deltas to OneShot's existing SSE channel as SUPPORT events
    // (do NOT mutate ProcessingEvent schema — use existing {scope,processor,message})
    if (event.type === "modelStreamUpdateEvent" && event.event?.delta?.type === "textDelta") {
      const delta = event.event.delta.text;
      text += delta;
      events.emit(runId, "ResearcherStream", "Running", {
        scope: "SUPPORT",
        message: delta,   // incremental token; frontend displays, ignores for state transitions
      });
    }
  }
}
```

**What changes for provider-agnostic streaming? Nothing extra.** `agent.stream()` is provider-agnostic because `VercelModel` implements Strands' `Model.stream()` for every Vercel provider. The SSE channel is already provider-agnostic (stage events, no provider fields). **Guardrail**: do not add provider/token fields to the locked `ProcessingEvent` schema (`processing-event.schema.json`; the frontend dedups on `event_id`). Emit tokens as `SUPPORT`-scoped events with `processor: "ResearcherStream"` using the existing `message` field.

