**Can we run both (OneShot native + Strands) temporarily?**
Yes — trivially. The Strands adapter sits **inside** Researcher Case E (`workflow.ts:111-136`), which already has Cases A–D (test draft, custom capability, function, direct model). Add a Case F ("Strands agent via VercelModel") gated by an env flag (e.g. `ONESHOT_RESEARCH_USE_STRANDS=1`), defaulting off. Both paths produce the same `ResearchBundle` (the boundary that feeds `buildResearchBundle` is unchanged), so the rest of the pipeline is identical. Run them side-by-side and diff `ResearchBundle` outputs for parity (exactly the plan's "Runtime parity drift → run old and new paths side-by-side with diff", `Refactor_plan.md:318`).

**Fallback plan if Strands doesn't fit?**
The adapter is additive and behind a flag, so fallback = set `ONESHOT_RESEARCH_USE_STRANDS=0` (or remove the one Case F block). The existing `generateText` path remains fully intact. `git revert` of the adapter commit restores the pre-Strands state — no other files depend on it.

