            const agent = new Agent({
              model: new VercelModel({ provider: activeModel }),
              systemPrompt: RESEARCHER_SYSTEM_PROMPT,
            });
            const result = await agent.invoke(promptText, {
              structuredOutputSchema: StructuredResearchDraftSchema,  // zod schema
            });
            draft = result.structuredOutput as StructuredResearchDraft;
            modelSource = `strands:${modelSource}`;
          } else {
            // Original path (unchanged)
            const result = await generateText({ model: activeModel, system: RESEARCHER_SYSTEM_PROMPT, prompt: promptText });
            draft = parseStructuredDraft(result.text);
          }
        } else {
          throw new WorkflowRootCauseError({ issue: "RESEARCH_CAPABILITY_UNAVAILABLE", ... });
        }
      }
```

### Differences highlighted

| Aspect | Before (`generateText`) | After (Strands `Agent` via `VercelModel`) |
|---|---|---|
| Model object | `activeModel` (LanguageModelV3) passed directly to `generateText` | Same `activeModel` wrapped in `new VercelModel({ provider: activeModel })` — **no new provider code** |
| Output parsing | `parseStructuredDraft(result.text)` — manual JSON parse + ```` ``` ```` cleanup + error → `RESEARCH_MODEL_OUTPUT_INVALID_JSON` | `result.structuredOutput` — zod-validated object; Strands **auto-retries on validation errors** |
| Provider switch | `resolveActiveIntegrationModel(projectRoot, preferredId)` (unchanged) | Identical — Strands adds no provider-specific code |
| Streaming | None (`generateText` is batch) | `agent.stream(prompt)` → `AsyncIterable<AgentStreamEvent>` available if wanted |
| Tools | None (deterministic evidence gather) | Optionally `tools: [tavilySearchTool]` for model-driven search (not minimum) |
| Downstream | `buildResearchBundle({ draft, gathered, modelSource, modelProvenance })` — **unchanged** | Identical — the `ResearchBundle` boundary is the contract; Strands stays inside the Researcher |
| Feature flag | — | `ONESHOT_RESEARCH_USE_STRANDS=1` (default off → both paths coexist) |

